Steps:
1. Inspect the project. Show me the folder listing of kart_racer and the
   kart_racer_flutter pubspec.yaml. Confirm the three packages exist. Change nothing.
2. Run the generated starter server and app once to confirm client and server connect.
   VERIFY the current Serverpod 4.1.2 start command and tell me what worked.
3. Add flutter_scene to kart_racer_flutter and run its init step. VERIFY against the
   package's current README. Pin the exact version in pubspec.yaml and record it in the
   status tracker in app.md.
4. Enable Flutter GPU for macOS desktop (and Android later). Explain what the flag does
   before applying it.
5. Render the package's built-in cube on macOS. No asset needed yet.
6. Register assets/3d/type-1.glb in pubspec.yaml, load it with Flutter Scene, and show it
   slowly rotating with a simple camera and light. Keep ALL Flutter Scene imports inside
   one folder (lib/game/rendering/), per the hard rules in app.md.
7. Run it on my Android phone. Tell me how to enable USB debugging if needed.
8. Measure frame rate with Flutter's performance overlay in profile or release mode
   (not debug) on the phone and write the number down.
9. Record in kart_racer_flutter/README.md: pinned versions, exact run commands (with
   the GPU flag), the measured frame rate, and the model's scale and facing direction.
   Add type-1.glb to assets/LICENSES.md with its source and license (ask me if I did
   not fill them in), then update CHANGELOG.md and the status tracker.

If the model appears huge, tiny, sideways or invisible, tell me and we will fix the
scale and orientation convention together. Do not silently rescale it in code without
telling me.

If something fails, stop and report the exact error, the package version and the device.
Do not switch rendering approaches without asking me.

